# Mini AI Documentation Project — Python Installation Guide

## Aim
Use AI to prepare professional documentation.

## Problem Statement
Prepare documentation for installing Python.

## Project Structure
```
Module1_Project/
│
├── Introduction.md     # Introduction + Software Requirements
├── Installation.md     # Installation Steps, Verification Steps, Troubleshooting, Conclusion
├── FAQ.md              # Frequently Asked Questions
├── Images/             # Screenshots referenced in the documentation (add your own)
└── README.md           # This file — project overview
```

## How to Use This Documentation
1. Start with `Introduction.md` to understand what Python is and confirm your system meets the software requirements.
2. Follow `Installation.md` for step-by-step installation instructions (Windows, macOS, Linux), how to verify the install, and how to troubleshoot common issues.
3. Check `FAQ.md` for quick answers to common questions.
4. Place any installation screenshots inside the `Images/` folder and reference them from the Markdown files (e.g. `![Verify Install](Images/verify_install.png)`).

